      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لَهُ بِأَيِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ يُعْلَمُ الْمُؤْمِنُ بِأَنَّهُ مُؤْمِنٌ قَالَ بِالتَّسْلِيمِ لِلَّهِ وَ الرِّضَا فِيمَا وَرَدَ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ سُرُورٍ أَوْ سَخَطٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from his father, from Ibn Sinan, from the one who mentioned it, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup>, said, ‘I said to him<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup>, ‘By which thing does the <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span> know that he is a <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span>?’ He<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup> said: ‘By the submission to Allah<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">azwj</sup>, and the satisfaction regarding whatever traspires upon him, from the joy or anger’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. It is narrated from him from his father from ibn Sinan from those whom he has mentioned from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “I (the narrator) asked him, (abu ‘Abd Allah, recipient of divine supreme covenant), ‘By what means can a believer know that he is a believer?’ The Imam said, ‘(He can find out) by means of his submitting himself to Allah, and agreeing with whatever happiness or sadness that he may experience.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
